- G | go home; this street has voted one way for fifty years, so tick it all off | v: tradition, hedonism | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: doors logged that were never knocked; backfire: the organiser checks the sheets against the replies, and the names do not match | self_control: - | tribal: go back to your own fire; these hearths have always gone one way, and say you spoke at each | magic: go home; this lane has always voted one way, so mark it all as knocked | chance: 95
- W>B | report the hostile door to the organiser, so nobody wastes another evening there | v: conformity, achievement | tribal: tell the speaker's kin which hearth is closed, so nobody wastes another walk | chance: 65
- U>R | team up with a friend to find a quicker, livelier way through the street | v: stimulation, achievement | mark: made a friend | tribal: pair up with a friend to find a quicker, merrier way round the hearths | chance: 65
- B>G | bring along an old neighbour, since every door on the street opens to her | v: benevolence, power | tribal: bring along an old woman of these hearths, since every hearth welcomes her | chance: 75
- R>W | laugh it off with the others over chips afterwards, and come back next week | v: hedonism, conformity | habit | self_control: + | grants: canvassing | tribal: laugh it off with the others at the fire, and walk out again next moon | magic: laugh it off with the others at the tavern, and come back next week | chance: 92
- G>U | ask the old hands which streets slam doors, and why, before the next round | v: tradition, self-direction | door | grants: knowing every street | tribal: ask the old walkers which hearths turn their backs, and why | magic: ask the faction's old hands which lanes shut their doors, and why | chance: 80
works: The next door opens, and the woman behind it talks for twenty minutes and promises her vote.
works: By the end of the evening the sheet is full, and the slammed door is a story to laugh about.
fails: Three more doors stay shut, and {N} walks home soaked and wondering what the point is.
fails: The man behind the slammed door complains to the candidate's people about the knocking.

== the candidate remembers your name
tier: everyday
rate: 0.2
times: per campaign volunteer: once or twice a campaign (estimate)
stages: child juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 14-100
calls: BRG
holds: campaign volunteer
