- G | ask the candidate to come and meet the neighbours on your street | v: benevolence, tradition | tribal: ask the speaker to come and sit at your family's hearth | magic: ask the candidate to come and meet the neighbours in your lane | chance: 45
- W>B | ask the candidate for a written reference for your applications | v: achievement, conformity | tribal: ask the speaker to give his word for your walking before the elders | magic: ask the candidate for a letter under seal, to show the guilds | chance: 70
- U>R | ask to join the inner team next time, to see the real work up close | v: stimulation, self-direction | door | tribal: ask to walk with the speaker's own circle next season, to see how it is done | magic: ask to join the faction's inner circle next season, to see the real work up close | chance: 60
- B>G | ask the candidate to sponsor your party membership, and say you mean to stand | v: achievement, security | identity | aims: party member | tribal: ask the speaker to bind you to the faction, and say you mean to speak at the fire one day | magic: ask the candidate to sponsor your oath to the faction, and say you mean to stand one day | chance: 90
- R>W | promise there and then to run the street team next time | v: benevolence, conformity | binds | tribal: promise there and then to lead the hearth-walkers next time | magic: promise there and then to lead the lane runners next time | chance: 85
- G>U | ask the old agent who has run every campaign here to pass on the trade | v: tradition, achievement | mark: learned a skill | grants: campaigning | tribal: ask the old hearth-walker who has served every speaker here to pass on the craft | magic: ask the old faction hand who has run every campaign here to pass on the trade | chance: 75
works: The candidate's thanks are real, and {N} walks home through the dark streets light as air.
works: The next week a message comes asking {N} to help again, this time with a bigger part.
fails: By morning the candidate has shaken a hundred hands, and the moment is gone.
