# ---------------------------------------------------------------- polling-station volunteer: calls UB / WRG (cycle s3)

== a voter not on the list
tier: everyday
rate: 0.5
times: per polling-station volunteer: on most election days at a busy station; about 3 lives in 100 work a polling station (catalogue share; estimate)
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-95
calls: UB
holds: polling-station volunteer
tone: trouble
life: community
horizon: moment
roles: elder, colleague, friend
earth: a voter at the desk in the school hall is not on the register, and the queue behind her is growing
tribal: a stranger from another band wants to cast a pebble at the gathering, and no one at the stones can vouch for her
magic: a voter with no seal on her papers wants a lot from the warded urn, and the queue behind her is growing
scene: An old woman at the desk in the school hall has voted at this station for forty years, she says, and today she is not on the register. The queue behind her reaches the door.
scene W: The rules are clear: no name, no ordinary ballot. The rules are also what keep every other vote in the box honest.
scene U: {N} runs a finger down the register twice. Her name is missing between two neighbours who are there: a clerical slip, or a move nobody recorded.
scene B: The presiding officer is on a break, and for the next ten minutes the decision is {Ns} own. {N} rather likes that.
scene R: The woman is near tears, and the man behind her is muttering. {N} feels the heat of the whole queue.
scene G: {N} knows her: she lives on the corner by the bakery and has done for decades. Everyone in this hall knows her.
- W | explain the rules gently, and offer her the sealed ballot kept for disputed votes | v: conformity, benevolence | tribal: explain the custom gently, and set her pebble aside until the elders have heard her | magic: explain the rules gently, and give her the sealed lot kept for disputed votes | chance: 70
- U | find the slip in the register, and ring the election office to check it | v: achievement | tribal: ask around the stones until someone remembers which band she came with | magic: find the slip in the roll, and send a runner to the Order's registry to check it | chance: 70
- B | make the call yourself while the officer is out, and stand by it | v: power, self-direction | identity | tribal: make the call yourself while the elders are away, and stand by it | magic: make the call yourself while the warden is out, and stand by it | chance: 70
- R | stand up for her to the grumbling queue, and give her all the time she needs | v: benevolence | chance: 90
- G | ask the old hands at the next table whether this has happened to her before | v: tradition | tribal: ask the old keepers of the stones whether this has happened to her before | chance: 70
- W>R | open a second desk to keep the queue moving while she is helped | v: benevolence, conformity | tribal: set out a second heap of stones, so the others can cast while she is heard | magic: open a second urn table, so the queue keeps moving while she is helped | chance: 75
- U>G | read the rules loosely enough to give her an ordinary ballot | v: benevolence, tradition | mark: broke the law | closed: law: an ordinary ballot given to a voter not on the register; backfire: the result is challenged, and the station's papers are pulled | tribal: read the custom loosely enough to let her cast a pebble with the band | magic: read the rules loosely enough to let her cast an ordinary lot | chance: 85
- B>W | wait for the presiding officer, so the decision goes on record as theirs | v: security, conformity | self_control: + | tribal: wait for the elders, so the choice is on record as theirs | magic: wait for the warden, so the decision is entered under the Order's seal | chance: 92
- R>U | ring her daughter to bring the card that proves where she is registered | v: benevolence, achievement | tribal: run to her kin's hearth to fetch someone who can vouch for her | magic: run to her lodging for the papers that prove her seal | chance: 55
- G>B | ask the neighbours in the queue to vouch for her, as people here always have | v: tradition, benevolence | identity | tribal: ask the families at the stones to vouch for her, as the bands always have | chance: 20
works: The mix-up is sorted, and she leaves with her vote cast and her dignity whole.
works: The queue moves again, and at the end of the day the presiding officer backs {Ns} call.
fails: She leaves without voting, telling everyone in the queue what she thinks of the station.
fails: The decision is questioned at the count, and {Ns} name goes into the incident book.

# Round 5, 2026-10-07 (P14): value tags read from the act on 1 option (check.py section 4).
== the count runs past midnight
tier: everyday
rate: 0.5
times: per polling-station volunteer who stays for the count: at most national counts (estimate)
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-95
calls: WRG
holds: polling-station volunteer
tone: mixed
life: community
horizon: moment
roles: colleague, elder, friend
earth: the count in the sports centre runs past midnight, and one bundle of ballots will not tally
tribal: the counting goes on by firelight, and one heap of pebbles keeps coming out different
magic: the urns are counted under the Order's lamps until dawn, and one tray of lots will not tally
scene: Past midnight in the sports centre: cold coffee and sore backs. One bundle of ballots has been counted three times and comes out three different ways.
scene W: Every ballot in that bundle is somebody's voice, and the count is the moment it is heard. {N} wants it right, not quick.
scene U: Three counts, three totals. {N} suspects two ballots stuck together, or one counted into the wrong pile.
scene B: The candidates' agents are watching every hand, and one of them is very keen for the count to end soon.
scene R: {N} is giddy with tiredness, laughing at nothing with {colleague}, and wide awake at the same time.
scene G: The same faces as every election: {elder} with the flask, the retired teacher who checks everyone's sums. {N} feels part of something old.
- W | sign the count sheet anyway, so the declaration is not held up | v: conformity, security | mark: hid a wrong | closed: law: a count signed off when it does not tally; backfire: a recount finds the gap, and the station's work is questioned | self_control: - | tribal: tell the elders the heap is right, so the choosing is not held up | magic: seal the tray's tally anyway, so the declaration is not held up | chance: 95
- U | spread the bundle out, and count it in tens, one ballot at a time | v: achievement | self_control: + | tribal: lay the pebbles out in rows of ten, one by one | magic: lay the lots out in rows of ten, one by one | chance: 90
- B | volunteer to lead the recount of the bundle, in front of the agents | v: achievement, power | self_control: + | tribal: offer to count the heap again yourself, in front of the speakers' kin | magic: offer to lead the recount of the tray, in front of the factions' agents | chance: 65
- R | crack a joke to wake the table up, and start the bundle again | v: hedonism, benevolence | chance: 80
- G | pour out the tea from the flask, and let the old hands set the pace | v: tradition, benevolence | tribal: pass round the warm broth, and let the old ones set the pace | magic: pour out the mulled wine, and let the old hands set the pace | chance: 80
- W>R | ask for a proper break for the whole table before the recount | v: benevolence, conformity | tribal: ask the elders for a rest by the fire before the heap is counted again | chance: 92
- U>G | show the youngest counters the old checking trick, the way the old hands taught it | v: tradition, achievement | tribal: show the youngest pebble-keepers the old way of checking a heap | magic: show the youngest counters the old checking trick of the Order's clerks | chance: 80
- B>W | insist the agents watch every recount closely, so nobody can cry foul later | v: security, conformity | tribal: make the speakers' kin watch every count closely, so nobody can cry foul later | magic: make the factions' agents watch every recount closely, so nobody can cry foul later | chance: 80
- R>U | stay on after the others go, until the last ballot makes sense | v: achievement, self-direction | self_control: + | tribal: stay by the fire after the others sleep, until the last pebble makes sense | magic: stay under the lamps after the others go, until the last lot makes sense | chance: 70
- G>B | let the oldest counter, thirty elections on, settle it for the table | v: tradition, power | tribal: let the oldest keeper of the stones settle it for everyone | chance: 65
works: The bundle finally tallies at a quarter to two, and the declaration goes ahead to applause.
works: The table walks out into the dawn together, tired and oddly proud.
fails: The recount drags on to four, and the agents' complaints go into the record.
fails: The bundle never tallies, and the whole count has to be checked again in the morning.

