== the annual meeting nobody comes to
tier: everyday
rate: 0.015
times: per local party officer: once a year; many branches struggle to reach a quorum outside election years; about 1 life in 100 holds a local party office (catalogue share; estimate)
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-100
calls: RG
holds: local party officer
tone: trouble
life: community
horizon: week
roles: friend, elder, colleague
earth: six people in a cold church hall for the branch's annual meeting, and the rules need ten to make a quorum
tribal: few families come to the faction's fire for the yearly choosing of its elders, and custom wants every hearth heard
magic: the faction's yearly meeting in an empty back room of the guild hall, and the charter wants ten sworn members
scene: Six people in a cold church hall, counting {N}, {elder} and the man who comes for the biscuits. The rules need ten to make a quorum, and the posts of chair and treasurer are both empty.
scene W: Without a quorum nothing the meeting decides is valid, and {N} knows the rulebook too well to pretend otherwise.
scene U: {N} has the membership list: a hundred and twelve names. Most joined in one rush three years ago and have not been seen since.
scene B: An empty branch is an opening: whoever fills the posts tonight runs the selection next year.
scene R: {N} looks at the rows of empty chairs and feels a stubborn spark: this branch is not dying on {Ns} watch.
scene G: {elder} has come to every annual meeting for forty years and remembers when this hall was full. The urn is on, as always.
- W | write down a quorum that was not there, so the branch can elect its officers | v: conformity, security | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: minutes that record members who were not there; backfire: an absent member reads the minutes and complains to the region | self_control: - | tribal: say every hearth was heard when few were, so the faction can choose its elders | magic: record ten sworn members in the faction's book when six were there | chance: 95
- U | propose merging with the next ward's branch, and hand over the books | v: achievement, security | drops: local party officer | tribal: propose joining the faction's fire to the next camp's, and hand over the tallies of gifts | magic: propose merging with the next ward's chapter, and hand over the books | chance: 70
- B | stand for chair and treasurer both, while nobody else wants them | v: power, achievement | identity | self_control: + | tribal: take both the faction's duties while no one else will | magic: take both the warden's chain and the coffer key while no one else will | chance: 90
- R | stand up and tell the six why the branch matters, and mean every word | v: stimulation, benevolence | tribal: stand up and tell the few at the fire why the faction matters, and mean every word | chance: 70
- G | keep the minutes faithfully, adjourn, and try again next month | v: tradition, conformity | habit | self_control: + | tribal: remember what was said faithfully, bank the fire, and try again next moon | chance: 95
- W>G | adjourn by the rules, and invite the whole ward to a summer fete instead | v: conformity, benevolence | door | tribal: put off the choosing by custom, and invite every hearth to a midsummer feast instead | magic: adjourn by the charter, and invite the whole ward to a street feast instead | chance: 60
- U>W | write to every lapsed member to ask what the branch should do for them | v: universalism, achievement | tribal: visit every hearth that stayed away, and ask what the faction should do for them | magic: write to every lapsed member to ask what the faction should do for them | chance: 35
- B>U | pay for an online meeting service yourself, so members can vote from home | v: self-direction, achievement | tribal: pay a runner from your own stores to carry each hearth's word to the fire | magic: pay a scribe from your own purse to carry sealed votes from members' homes | chance: 70
- R>B | ring your old school friends, and talk them into joining before the next meeting | v: benevolence, power | mark: made a friend | tribal: go to the friends you grew up with, and talk them into the faction before the next fire | chance: 50
- G>R | take the six across to the cafe, and make it a night worth coming back for | v: hedonism, benevolence | tribal: turn the gathering into a night of songs, so people want to come back | magic: move the six to the tavern next door, and make it a night people want back | chance: 65
works: The next meeting has fourteen people in it, and two of them are under thirty.
works: The posts are filled, and the branch has a proper chair for the first time in two years.
fails: The branch limps on for another year with six members and no treasurer.
fails: Word of the empty hall reaches the region, and the branch is merged with the next ward without being asked.

# Round 5, 2026-10-07 (P14): value tags read from the act on 1 option (check.py section 4).
== two members want the same nomination
tier: everyday
rate: 0.015
times: per local party officer a year: about 1 in 5, most of all in the year before local elections (estimate)
stages: juvenile young_adult adult mature elder
age: 16-100
calls: WUB
holds: local party officer
tone: trouble
life: community, friends
horizon: months
roles: friend, colleague, elder
earth: two members of the branch both want the nomination for the same council seat, and both ask for your backing
tribal: two of the faction's young want to be its voice at the fire, and both come to your hearth for your word
magic: two sworn members want the faction's seal for the same seat on the town council, and both ask for yours
scene: Two members, {friend} and {colleague}, both want the branch's nomination for the one winnable council seat. Both have rung {N} this week, and both have said, in nearly the same words, that they are counting on {N}.
scene W: {N} runs the selection, and whoever runs it must be seen to have no favourite. That is the whole of the job.
scene U: {N} has walked the ward with both. One is better on the doorstep, the other in the council chamber, and the seat needs both.
scene B: Whoever wins will owe {N} for the result. The branch's next ten years may turn on who that is.
scene R: {friend} has been {Ns} friend since school, and {N} badly wants to say so out loud.
scene G: {colleague} comes from a family that has run this branch for three generations, and {elder} expects it to go on that way.
- W | run a fair hustings and a secret ballot, and back neither in public | v: conformity, universalism | self_control: + | tribal: let both speak at the fire, let the families choose, and say nothing for either | magic: hold a fair disputation and a sealed ballot, and back neither openly | chance: 75
- U | score both against what the seat needs, and share the scores with the branch | v: achievement | identity | tribal: weigh both against what the band needs, and tell the faction plainly | chance: 60
- B | sign up a dozen new members who will vote for your choice | v: power | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: a meeting packed with members signed up for one vote; backfire: the region freezes the selection and audits the new members | tribal: bring a dozen kin into the faction just in time to stand behind your choice | magic: enrol a dozen new sworn members just in time to cast for your choice | chance: 80
- R | tell your old friend, straight out, that you are backing them | v: stimulation, benevolence | tribal: tell your old friend, straight out, that your word is theirs | chance: 95
- G | ask the oldest members which of the two the ward would trust | v: tradition | tribal: ask the oldest of the faction which of the two the hearths would trust | chance: 65
- W>G | broker an agreement that the loser gets the next seat that comes up | v: universalism, benevolence | binds | grants: settling disputes | tribal: broker an agreement that the other speaks at the next fire | magic: broker an agreement that the other gets the next seat that falls open | chance: 40
- U>W | write the selection rules down in full before anyone votes, and send them to both | v: conformity, achievement | binds | tribal: set out the custom for the choosing before anyone stands, and tell it to both | magic: write the rules of the choosing in full before any lot is cast, and send them to both | chance: 95
